r2
Usage: r2 [-A] FILE

The interactive front end of radare2 (the same binary under a shorter name).
`r2 FILE` drops you into its own prompt to explore a binary -- analyse it, list
its functions, disassemble, read its strings, edit its bytes.

	r2 FILE       open the binary in the r2 shell
	-A            auto-analyse on open
	inside: afl (functions), pdf @main (disassemble main), iz (strings), q (quit)

See also: radare2, file, binwalk
